  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Depreciation: depreciating every month or every few months (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A matatu costs Ksh \( {@P0@} \). Due to wear and tear, it depreciates by \( {@rd(r0)@}\% \) <strong>{@perw@}</strong>.</p>
<p>(a) How many depreciation periods are there in \( {@Y0@} \) years?</p>
<div>Number of periods \( = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Find the value of the matatu after \( {@Y0@} \) years, to the nearest shilling.</p>
<div>Value \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> The rate \( {@rd(r0)@}\% \) applies {@perw@}, which happens \( {@kk@} \) times a year, so in \( {@Y0@} \) years there are \( {@kk@} \times {@Y0@} = {@nper@} \) periods.</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong></p>
\[ A = P\left(1 - \frac{r}{100}\right)^n = {@P0@}\left(1 - \frac{ {@rd(r0)@} }{100}\right)^{ {@nper@} } = {@round(A0)@}. \]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[rd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else float(v);
pp : rand([[12, "every month"], [4, "every 3 months"], [2, "every 6 months"]]);
kk : pp[1];
perw : pp[2];
r0 : if kk = 12 then rand([1, 3/2, 2]) else if kk = 4 then rand([3, 4, 5]) else rand([5, 6, 8]);
Y0 : rand([1, 2, 3]);
P0 : rand([1800000, 2400000, 3000000, 3500000]);
nper : kk*Y0;
A0 : P0*(1 - r0/100)^nper;
w_years : P0*(1 - r0/100)^Y0;            /* used the years as the number of periods */
w_line  : P0*(1 - r0*nper/100);          /* straight-line */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
